The hstr_copy function "hstr_copy.h"

    Description

            The hstr_copy function copies the short string
            specified by #1 to the array specified by #0,
            the target.

    Returns

            If the objects speficied by the arguments
            overlap and if the result of copying alters the
            array specified by #1, a positive value is
            returned, indicating an error. Otherwise, if the
            initial HSTR_SIZE_MAX characters of the array
            specified by #1 are not a string, a negative
            value is returned, indicating atypical
            behavior---#1 does not specify a short string.
            Otherwise, a zero value is returned, indcating
            success.
